From 801743f1d02cb2b7dda9dd430de021b235171989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:00:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): canonicalize renamed GitHub repo URLs in
 respawn-guard PR matching [daveey]

daveey/hermes was transferred to example-org/hermes (same repo id).
Owners still checkpoint PRs as https://github.com/daveey/hermes/pull/N while
reviewers record the canonical URL from gh, so _named_prs failed closed and
active_pr held implementers whose exact-head review handoff was complete
(t_01a1cca14b7a62d3, PR 1208).

norm_pr is now the single PR comparison key: lowercased, no trailing slash,
https scheme, and a known renamed repo mapped to its canonical owner/repo
(built-in daveey/hermes -> example-org/hermes, extensible with
kanban.github_repo_aliases; invalid entries ignored, unreadable config keeps
built-ins, map cached 60 s). It is used by the review checkpoint, _named_prs
(URL and repo#N refs), resumes_review, is_review_result, holding_urls and
foreign-contract matching, hold release scope/publications/released_after,
and pr_state/rejection caching. Matching never falls back to number-only
across repos.

Proof:
- RED on origin/main: 21 of 33 new alias tests and the hold-release scope
  test fail; GREEN: 46 importing test files, 2105 passed.
- 22 mutants on every added condition: all killed.
- Replay old vs new active_pr_reason (pr_state stubbed OPEN, pinned clock)
  over the local Board replica boards (default/hermes/bb/askeve: 87 live
  cards naming PRs) and the hub kanban DB copy (50 cards): 2 changed, both
  held -> released and both the target shape: t_01a1cca14b7a62d3 (alias
  checkpoint, canonical reviewed_pr, request_changes at exact head) and
  t_01a1cde626be2ada (canonical checkpoint, alias reviewed_pr, same). No card
  moved to held.
